  - q: "What services does Abraham Otieno offer?"
    a: "Six: executive time optimisation (EA scope), operational accountability systems, market entry and joint-venture coordination, distributed team reliability, project execution and stakeholder alignment, and executive communication. Most engagements combine two or three, scoped on the discovery call."
  - q: "Can I hire you for one service or is it all bundled?"
    a: "Single services are fine. A market-entry project or a systems build can run standalone. Ongoing engagements usually blend an EA-scope service with an operations or chief-of-staff one, because that is where the leverage compounds."
  - q: "How are services priced?"
    a: "Three formats. Hourly retainer (10 to 20 hrs/week) for ongoing EA support. Monthly retainer for chief-of-staff or operations-partner scope. Project-based fixed fee for market entry, system builds, and one-off launches. Rates are senior-operator level but Nairobi-based, well below US or UK equivalents. Exact pricing is agreed on the discovery call."
  - q: "Do you work remotely, and do the time zones line up?"
    a: "Every service is delivered remotely from Nairobi (EAT, UTC+3), which covers European hours live and the US East Coast for a working day. US founders get a pre-staged morning: work moves while they sleep."
  - q: "How quickly can a service start?"
    a: "Most engagements start within one week of the discovery call: a 90-minute kickoff, then a documented operating rhythm in place by the end of week one."
  - q: "Which service do I need if I'm not sure?"
    a: "Start with the bottleneck, not the title. Losing your week to coordination points to time optimisation. Commitments slipping through the team points to accountability systems. A stalled initiative points to project execution. The discovery call settles it in 30 minutes."
